\section{The MIEB Benchmark}
\paragraph{Overview.} MIEB comprises 130 tasks in 8 categories (\autoref{tab:MIEB big tasks}): Retrieval (45 tasks), Document Understanding (10), Linear Probing (22), Clustering (5), Zero-shot Classification (23), Compositionality (7), Vision-centric QA (6) and Visual STS (9). Retrieval and Visual STS cover multiple languages (38 in total; Visual STS covers 12 languages in its English and multilingual subsets); document understanding covers 2 languages, and the remaining categories are English.

\paragraph{Data curation.} Tasks are curated from established datasets: retrieval suites in the style of M-BEIR~\cite{wei2023uniir}, multilingual retrieval (xFlickr\&CO, XM3600, WIT), compositionality (ARO, Winoground~\cite{Thrush_2022_CVPR}), ImageNet-1k and fine-grained classification sets, clustering, document-understanding retrieval in the style of ViDoRe~\cite{faysse2024colpali}, and STS~\cite{cer-etal-2017-semeval,agirre-etal-2013-sem}. MIEB reuses the human annotations of the source datasets; Visual STS inherits human similarity labels from STS. No new human annotation is collected. MIEB enforces standardized formats, versioning and evaluation scripts for reproducibility. Adding a model requires a simple wrapper producing image and text embeddings, and a new dataset is specified by a single metadata file.

\paragraph{Visual STS.} Existing STS tasks (STS12--17, STS-b and cross-lingual/multilingual variants) are rendered as images, and the similarity of the embeddings of a rendered sentence pair is correlated with human scores. This measures whether a vision encoder can read and semantically understand text in images.

\paragraph{Protocols.} \emph{Retrieval}: documents are ranked by similarity to queries (inputs and corpora may be images, text or interleaved); the metric is nDCG@10 (sometimes recall@1 or MAP@5), and document understanding uses nDCG@5. \emph{Linear probing}: logistic regression (at most 100 iterations) on frozen embeddings with $k=16$ examples per class by default; accuracy. \emph{Zero-shot classification}: labels are turned into prompts (``a photo of \{label\}'') and the top-1 class by similarity is predicted; accuracy. \emph{Clustering}: $k$-means with $k$ equal to the number of ground-truth classes; normalized mutual information (NMI). \emph{Compositionality}: distinguishing positives from hard negatives built by perturbing attributes, relations or order; accuracy. \emph{Visual STS}: Spearman correlation $\rho$ with human scores per dataset. Linear probing keeps the encoder frozen and is thus still considered zero-shot with respect to the encoder.

\paragraph{Interleaved inputs and multilinguality.} Interleaved inputs are native for MLLM-based models; for the other models, interleaved embeddings are formed by summing image and text embeddings. Multilingual analyses report the mean and the variance across languages.

