\paragraph{MIEB-lite.} To reduce cost we remove redundant tasks using inter-task performance correlations. Tasks are pruned iteratively when their average correlation exceeds 0.5 (11 tasks) and 0.45 (32 tasks); in addition, UMAP~\cite{mcinnes2018umap} with HDBSCAN~\cite{mcinnes2017hdbscan} yields 17 interpretable task clusters, from which representative tasks are chosen to preserve category and difficulty coverage. The resulting 51-task MIEB-lite agrees strongly with the full benchmark over 38 models (Spearman 0.992, Pearson 0.986).

\section{Models}
We evaluate 50 models in three families. \emph{Vision-only self-supervised} models: MoCo-v3~\cite{chen2021empirical} and DINOv2~\cite{oquab2024dinov2}. \emph{CLIP-style language-supervised} encoders: CLIP~\cite{radford2021learning}, OpenCLIP~\cite{cherti2023reproducible}, SigLIP~\cite{zhai2023sigmoid} (including a multilingual variant), ALIGN~\cite{jia2021scaling}, DataComp-CLIP~\cite{gadre2024datacomp}, EVA-CLIP~\cite{sun2023eva} and VISTA~\cite{zhou2024vista}. \emph{MLLM-based embedding} models: E5-V~\cite{jiang2024e5}, VLM2Vec (Full and LoRA)~\cite{jiang2024vlm2vec} and the commercial Voyage-multimodal-3~\cite{voyagemultimodal2024voyage}.

\section{Implementation Details}
All models are run through the same wrapper interface and evaluation scripts, with every model and dataset versioned in the codebase and leaderboard. Runtimes are measured in NVIDIA H100 GPU hours. Unless stated otherwise, linear probing uses $k=16$ shots per class. Non-native interleaved inputs use summed image and text embeddings.

