\paragraph{Overall.} \autoref{tab: overall results top 20.} reports results by category for the top 20 models. By the overall mean over 130 tasks, Voyage-multimodal-3 is best (62.5), followed by E5-V (58.2) and siglip-so400m-patch14-384 (57.1). Yet no model is best everywhere (\autoref{tab:leaders}). CLIP-style encoders lead on retrieval (best single score 41.5 for CLIP-ViT-bigG-14-laion2B; SigLIP-so400m 40.8), clustering (NMI 92.4, EVA02-CLIP-bigE-14-plus), zero-shot classification (70.8, SigLIP-so400m-patch14-384 and EVA02-CLIP-bigE-14-plus) and 16-shot linear probing (86.0, EVA02-CLIP-bigE-14-plus). MLLM-based models lead elsewhere: compositionality (E5-V, 46.3), vision-centric QA (VLM2Vec-Full 62.1, VLM2Vec-LoRA 62.0), document understanding (Voyage 71.1; E5-V 62.7 is the best open-source model) and English Visual STS (Voyage 81.8, E5-V 79.3). MLLM-based models underperform on fine-grained classification and clustering, suggesting less precise low-level visual granularity.

