\paragraph{Visual STS as a proxy for text-in-image ability.} \autoref{tab:E5-V STS analysis} compares E5-V on regular STS (average 86.0, numbers from \citet{jiang2024e5}) with Visual STS (79.3): E5-V approaches OCR-level reading but a gap remains. CLIP-family models achieve high Visual STS, whereas vision-only self-supervised models are near random. Furthermore, encoder Visual STS correlates strongly (above 99\% on OCR/TextVQA-like tasks) with the MLLM results on Cambrian~\cite{tong2024cambrian} benchmarks that rely on visual text understanding (\autoref{fig:corr}), which makes it possible to select vision encoders for an MLLM without a full MLLM evaluation.

